    {
      "id": "SbgHAHbyom5vu5LDuedWB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 856.8296591605597,
      "y": 611.0836898064674,
      "width": 877.8994140625,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 601426974,
      "version": 1105,
      "versionNonce": 1071832898,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787558156626,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Association:\n    - one object connected to another object.\n    --> An Order is associated with Customer.\n    - In state, stores the reference of another object of class.\n    -  one-to-one: A user has a Profile\n       one-to-many: one customer can place many orders\n       many-to-one: many students learns from one teacher\n       many-to-many: One student has many courses, one course has many students\n    - Diagram = Student -> Teacher\n2. Aggregation:\n    - has-a relationship with weak ownership\n    --> Engineer team has a developers, but if team removed still developers can exists\n            independently\n    - Diagram = Playlists <>-- has a Song\n3. Composition:\n    - has-a relationship with strong ownership\n    --> Car has a Engine, but engine fails - car fails.\n    - Diagram = Car   -- contains Engine\n4. Dependency:\n    - one class uses another class to perform its work. weak relationship than association\n    --> An OrderService may depend on an inventory service.\n    - Diagram = Printer --uses--> Document",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Association:\n    - one object connected to another object.\n    --> An Order is associated with Customer.\n    - In state, stores the reference of another object of class.\n    -  one-to-one: A user has a Profile\n       one-to-many: one customer can place many orders\n       many-to-one: many students learns from one teacher\n       many-to-many: One student has many courses, one course has many students\n    - Diagram = Student -> Teacher\n2. Aggregation:\n    - has-a relationship with weak ownership\n    --> Engineer team has a developers, but if team removed still developers can exists\n            independently\n    - Diagram = Playlists <>-- has a Song\n3. Composition:\n    - has-a relationship with strong ownership\n    --> Car has a Engine, but engine fails - car fails.\n    - Diagram = Car   -- contains Engine\n4. Dependency:\n    - one class uses another class to perform its work. weak relationship than association\n    --> An OrderService may depend on an inventory service.\n    - Diagram = Printer --uses--> Document",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
