    {
      "id": "iSNmVbmOeKKvgF1FyuQr_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3196.1359528504677,
      "y": -580.8279135793956,
      "width": 1068.29931640625,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 614079938,
      "version": 502,
      "versionNonce": 730320478,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787558156626,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "S: Single Responsibility Principle\n    - A class should have one-and-only-one responsibility\nO: Open/Closed Principle\n    - Class/Methods/functions should be Open for extension and Close for modifications\n    - Use strategy pattern, interface \nL: Liskov substitution Principle\n    - If C is a subtype of P, then objects of type P may be replaced with objects of type C without altering \n        any of the desirable properties of that program (correctness, task performed, etc.).\nI: Interface Segregation Principle\n    - Clients should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use.\n    - Create separate interfaces depends on methods then should use\nD: Dependency Inversion Principle\n    - High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules. Both should depend on abstractions\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "S: Single Responsibility Principle\n    - A class should have one-and-only-one responsibility\nO: Open/Closed Principle\n    - Class/Methods/functions should be Open for extension and Close for modifications\n    - Use strategy pattern, interface \nL: Liskov substitution Principle\n    - If C is a subtype of P, then objects of type P may be replaced with objects of type C without altering \n        any of the desirable properties of that program (correctness, task performed, etc.).\nI: Interface Segregation Principle\n    - Clients should not be forced to depend on methods they do not use.\n    - Create separate interfaces depends on methods then should use\nD: Dependency Inversion Principle\n    - High-level modules should not depend on low-level modules. Both should depend on abstractions\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
